          "role": "system",
          "content": "You are a formal verification engineer.\nWrite one declarative JSON contract for the `place_order` operation.\nOutput JSON only, without markdown or explanatory prose.\nAll monetary values are integer cents.\n\nState variables:\n- `card_limit` (number)\n- `cart` (multiset)\n- `cart_size` (number)\n- `cart_subtotal` (number)\n- `checkout_total` (number)\n- `coupon_code` (option)\n- `logged_in` (bool)\n- `order_items` (multiset)\n- `order_payment_method` (option)\n- `order_size` (number)\n- `order_status` (text)\n- `order_total` (number)\n- `payment_method` (option)\n- `shipping_address` (option)\n- `stock` (multiset)\n- `wallet_balance` (number)\n\nPublic configuration sets:\n- `addresses`\n- `coupon_codes`\n- `items`\n- `payment_methods`\n\nTerm literals:\n- {\"var\": \"<state var>\", \"when\": \"before\"|\"after\"} — a state variable. \"when\" defaults to \"before\" and may only be \"after\" in a postcondition.\n- {\"const\": true|1|\"text\"|null} — a literal boolean, integer, string, or null.\n- {\"multiset\": {\"<item>\": <count>, ...}} — a literal item multiset.\n\nTerm operators:\n- `count`: {\"op\": \"count\", \"of\": t, \"item\": \"<item>\"} — units of one item in a multiset.\n- `total`: {\"op\": \"total\", \"of\": t} — total units in a multiset.\n- `difference`: {\"op\": \"difference\", \"left\": t, \"right\": t} — the first multiset minus the second; has no value if any line would go negative.\n- `subtract`: {\"op\": \"subtract\", \"left\": t, \"right\": t} — numeric subtraction.\n\nFormula operators:\n- `const`: {\"op\": \"const\", \"value\": true} — a literal truth value.\n- `and`: {\"op\": \"and\", \"args\": [f, ...]} — every listed formula holds.\n- `or`: {\"op\": \"or\", \"args\": [f, ...]} — at least one listed formula holds.\n- `not`: {\"op\": \"not\", \"arg\": f} — the formula does not hold.\n- `is_true`: {\"op\": \"is_true\", \"arg\": t} — a boolean term is true.\n- `is_null`: {\"op\": \"is_null\", \"arg\": t} — an optional term is unset (null).\n- `is_empty`: {\"op\": \"is_empty\", \"arg\": t} — an item multiset has no units.\n- `eq`: {\"op\": \"eq\", \"left\": t, \"right\": t} — two terms of the same kind are equal.\n- `ne`: {\"op\": \"ne\", \"left\": t, \"right\": t} — two terms of the same kind differ.\n- `lt`: {\"op\": \"lt\", \"left\": t, \"right\": t} — a number is strictly smaller.\n- `le`: {\"op\": \"le\", \"left\": t, \"right\": t} — a number is smaller or equal.\n- `gt`: {\"op\": \"gt\", \"left\": t, \"right\": t} — a number is strictly greater.\n- `ge`: {\"op\": \"ge\", \"left\": t, \"right\": t} — a number is greater or equal.\n- `in_set`: {\"op\": \"in_set\", \"value\": t, \"set\": \"<config set>\"} — a text/optional term is a member of a configured set; an unset value is never a member.\n- `covers`: {\"op\": \"covers\", \"available\": t, \"required\": t} — the first multiset holds at least every quantity of the second.\n- `unchanged`: {\"op\": \"unchanged\", \"vars\": [\"<state var>\", ...]} — every listed variable has the same value before and after (postcondition only).\n\nRules:\n- The precondition may read only before-state variables.\n- The postcondition may compare before and after variables.\n- `unchanged` is valid only in the postcondition.\n- Use only the listed operators and state variables.\n- Return exactly one complete JSON object."
        },
        {
          "role": "user",
          "content": "Synthesize the exact applicability and effect contract for `place_order`.\nThe storefront is deterministic, but not every policy boundary is stated explicitly.\nCounterexamples, when supplied later, are observations from the storefront.\n\nAgent-visible configuration:\n- Items and unit prices: {'book': 2400, 'gift': 2500}\n- Cart capacity: 2\n- Selectable payment methods: ['card']\n- Selectable addresses: ['home']\n- Selectable coupon codes: ['save500']\n- Initial wallet balance: 10000\n- Card limit: 10000\n\nThe state exposes `cart_subtotal` and `checkout_total` as storefront-computed values.\nSelecting a payment method, address, or coupon does not prove that checkout will accept it.\nA successful order records payment, populates the order slot, and may update checkout-related state.\nInfer the exact conditions and frame/effect relations.\n\nNeutral JSON envelope:\n{\n  \"skill\": \"place_order\",\n  \"notes\": \"schema envelope only; not a candidate contract\",\n  \"precondition\": {\n    \"op\": \"const\",\n    \"value\": true\n  },\n  \"postcondition\": {\n    \"op\": \"const\",\n    \"value\": true\n  }\n}\n\nOutput only the complete JSON contract:"
